  scope: package-level step-parser helpers that convert parsed automation step DTOs (trigger, condition, action) into the domain models.AutomationStep* payload shapes used both for persistence (database.AutomationStepWrite) and for downstream FSM/evaluator/executor consumption, plus the small request-inspection helper that returns the first trigger kind on a parsed createAutomationRequest. These three helpers form a tightly cohesive group: automationStepWrites orchestrates the parse, automationStepPayloadModel performs the per-DTO-type → models.AutomationStep* conversion (the single dispatch point for trigger/condition/action step parsing), and firstTriggerKind inspects the parsed request for audit logging. The "// ── Create ──" section header comment stays in the original file because it now introduces only the Create handler (and is still semantically correct).
  identifiers_moved (all unexported; preserved in source order — extracted from original lines 202..325):
    automation_handler_step_parsers.go (3 funcs, all unexported):
      - func automationStepWrites(req *createAutomationRequest) ([]database.AutomationStepWrite, error)
          Orchestrator: builds persistence-shape step writes from a parsed automation request by invoking the persistence-order step list helper, the step-order computation helper (both moved to automation_handler_decode.go in prompt 03 and resolved cross-file in package api), and automationStepPayloadModel for each typed step. Wraps per-step parse errors with "step %d: %w".
      - func automationStepPayloadModel(step automationTypedStep) (any, error)
          Single dispatch point: 12-arm type switch over automationTypedStep.Payload covering all four trigger DTO types (signal/geofence/schedule/event), all four condition DTO types (signal/time-window/geofence/other-automation), all four action DTO types (command/notify/set-setting/call-automation), and a default unsupported-type error. Performs strings.TrimSpace normalisation on identifier-shaped fields, defaults empty CommandParams to `{}` JSON, defaults empty Timezone to "UTC", and parses HH:MM:SS clock fields via parseAutomationClockTime (lives in automation_handler_decode.go, same package — cross-file reference unchanged).
      - func firstTriggerKind(req *createAutomationRequest) string
          Inspector: returns the Kind of the first parsed trigger, or "" for nil or empty Triggers slice. Used by Create/Update for audit-log "trigger_kind" field.
